Section 1: Description of the Container#
The Student Course Registration System is a proposed cloud-based web application that lets students view courses, enroll in available sections, and review their schedules. The application follows a three-tier architecture: (1) presentation tier (browser and HTML templates), (2) application tier (Flask web service running in a Docker container), and (3) data tier (a shared PostgreSQL database). Other common architectural templates include client-server and microservices; this project selects three-tier architecture for its separation of concerns.

Cloud-based software runs on remote computing infrastructure and can be accessed over a network. Docker packages the application and its dependencies into an isolated container. A Docker image is the read-only package used to create a container; the Docker daemon is the background service that manages images, containers, and networks. A daemon is generally a background process providing a service.

The application container contains Python, Flask, application source code, HTML templates, and installed Python packages. The PostgreSQL database runs separately as a shared database service, not inside the application container. The application connects using environment variables, such as DATABASE_URL, rather than storing credentials in source control.

